   "id": "1a1374cf",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Telecom customer churn: who is about to leave, and is it worth calling them?\n",
    "\n",
    "A telecom operator loses customers every quarter. Calling a customer with a retention offer costs money, and the offer only works on some of them. So there are two questions:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Which customers are most likely to leave?** (a prediction problem)\n",
    "2. **For which of them is the offer worth its price?** (a decision problem)\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook answers both, step by step, on the IBM Telco customer churn dataset (a fictional dataset: 7,043 customers, 50 columns). The costs used for the decision are assumptions, not real data.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Needs:** `pandas`, `numpy`, `matplotlib`, `scikit-learn`, `shap`, `joblib`, and the file `telco.csv` next to this notebook.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Contents**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Setup\n",
    "2. Load and inspect the data\n",
    "3. Clean the missing values\n",
    "4. Choose which customers to keep\n",
    "5. Explore what drives churn\n",
    "6. Build the features\n",
    "7. Baseline and train/test split\n",
    "8. Compare five models\n",
    "9. Choose the decision threshold\n",
    "10. Why do customers leave?\n",
    "11. What does the model rely on? (SHAP)\n",
    "12. Sensitivity check\n",
    "13. Final test on the held-out set\n",
    "14. Save the model for the app\n",
    "15. Conclusions and limits"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "27c671af",
   "metadata": {},
