   "source": [
    "**A trap in the data.** In the row `(0, 3]`, the churn rate is 100%: every customer with 3 months of tenure or less has left. That is not real behaviour. It comes from my own filter: the customers with a short tenure who *stayed* were the \"Joined\" ones, and I just removed them. Only the ones who left remain.\n",
    "\n",
    "A model trained on this would learn \"short tenure means gone\" and look much better than it really is. So the model must only be used for customers with **more than 3 months** of tenure, and we remove the others too."
