  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d8419a1b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Build the features\n",
    "\n",
    "A model only reads numbers, so every column has to become a number:\n",
    "\n",
    "- numeric columns are kept as they are;\n",
    "- yes/no columns become 1 and 0;\n",
    "- categories (offer, internet type, contract, payment method) become one 0/1 column per value, dropping one value (`drop_first=True`) because it is implied by the others.\n",
    "\n",
    "Everything is in one function, `build_features`, so the same steps can be reused on new customers.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Columns left out, and why**\n",
    "\n",
    "| Columns | Reason |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| `Customer Status`, `Churn Label`, `Churn Score`, `Churn Category`, `Churn Reason` | They describe the outcome, or may be computed from it (data leakage). |\n",
    "| `Satisfaction Score`, `CLTV` | May depend on the outcome too, so I left them out as a precaution. |\n",
    "| `Customer ID`, `City`, `State`, `Country`, `Zip Code`, `Latitude`, `Longitude`, `Quarter` | Identifiers and location. |\n",
    "| `Total Charges`, `Total Revenue`, `Total Long Distance Charges` | Cumulative totals that mostly repeat tenure x monthly charge. |\n",
    "| `Senior Citizen`, `Under 30`, `Dependents`, `Internet Service` | Already contained in `Age`, `Number of Dependents` and `Internet Type`. |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 13,
   "id": "d29e44a1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Features: (5992, 36)\n",
      "int64      33\n",
      "float64     3\n",
      "Name: count, dtype: int64\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "yes_no_cols = [\n",
    "    \"Married\", \"Referred a Friend\", \"Phone Service\", \"Multiple Lines\",\n",
    "    \"Online Security\", \"Online Backup\", \"Device Protection Plan\",\n",
    "    \"Premium Tech Support\", \"Streaming TV\", \"Streaming Movies\",\n",
    "    \"Streaming Music\", \"Unlimited Data\", \"Paperless Billing\",\n",
    "]\n",
    "numeric_cols = [\n",
    "    \"Age\", \"Number of Dependents\", \"Population\", \"Number of Referrals\",\n",
    "    \"Tenure in Months\", \"Avg Monthly Long Distance Charges\", \"Avg Monthly GB Download\",\n",
    "    \"Monthly Charge\", \"Total Refunds\", \"Total Extra Data Charges\",\n",
    "]\n",
    "category_cols = [\"Offer\", \"Internet Type\", \"Contract\", \"Payment Method\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def build_features(data):\n",
    "    X = data[numeric_cols].copy()\n",
    "    X[\"Male\"] = (data[\"Gender\"] == \"Male\").astype(int)\n",
    "    for c in yes_no_cols:\n",
    "        X[c] = (data[c] == \"Yes\").astype(int)\n",
    "    dummies = pd.get_dummies(data[category_cols], drop_first=True).astype(int)\n",
    "    return pd.concat([X, dummies], axis=1)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "X = build_features(df)\n",
    "y = df[\"churned\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Features:\", X.shape)\n",
    "print(X.dtypes.value_counts())"
   ]
  },
