    "Things to keep in mind when reading this table:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Logistic regression, random forest and SVM were trained with class weights and gradient boosting was not, so their **recall is not directly comparable**. AUC is the fairer comparison.\n",
    "- The gap between the best models can be smaller than the noise of cross-validation. Gradient boosting is kept as the model for the rest of the notebook.\n",
    "\n",
    "**My reading:**\n",
    " Gradient boosting has the best AUC (0.910), but logistic regression is very close (0.902), so the gap may be within the noise of cross-validation. I keep gradient boosting for the rest of the project, with the idea that a simpler model would also have been a fair choice. Accuracy alone would have been misleading: the baseline that predicts \"nobody leaves\" already reaches 0.788, so what matters is how well each model ranks the customers who really leave."
