    "## 11. What does the model rely on? (SHAP)\n",
    "\n",
    "SHAP gives, for every customer and every variable, a **push** toward \"leaves\" (right) or \"stays\" (left). Each dot is a customer, the colour is the value of the variable (red = high, blue = low), and the variables are sorted by importance.\n",
    "\n",
    "SHAP explains **the model**, not the real world: a variable that pushes the risk up is not necessarily the cause of churn."
   ]
